From df0f1a74ec2e8d2535beb3633b99b49619e860e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: d-b-c-e <anthony.mason1@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 14:33:05 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 07/24] POC: overlay is an owned top-level popup, not a child
 window

WS_CLIPCHILDREN never worked because MAME's gdi renderer caches its
window DC - clip regions are fixed at DC acquisition, so neither the
style bit nor SWP_FRAMECHANGED reach it, and its blit kept punching
through (rig evidence: alternating stretched/letterboxed frames, made
distinguishable by -nokeepaspect). An owned WS_POPUP is composited by
DWM and occludes the owner absolutely - no GDI clipping involved.
NOACTIVATE+TRANSPARENT+DISABLED keep keyboard focus, mouse and
DirectInput foreground on MAME's window; the loop tracks the owner's
client rect in screen coords and hides on minimize.
---
 src/mame/midway/midvunit_v.cpp | 45 +++++++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 17 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/mame/midway/midvunit_v.cpp b/src/mame/midway/midvunit_v.cpp
index d9cac7bb..296b263a 100644
--- a/src/mame/midway/midvunit_v.cpp
+++ b/src/mame/midway/midvunit_v.cpp
@@ -466,26 +466,26 @@ void thread_main()
 	for (int i = 0; i < 100 && !parent; i++) { Sleep(100); parent = find_mame_window(); }
