Subject: [PATCH 12/24] CRT pass: mask + scanlines + curvature in the palette
 stage, F9 live toggle

PAL_FS gains a uCrt-gated block (uCrt=0 is the untouched raw path; the
exact-mode invariant compares the index buffer upstream anyway, re-verified
100.0000%): gentle barrel warp with black outside the glass, gaussian
scanlines per source line with brightness-dependent beam width, 3-tap
horizontal beam softness, two-phase magenta/green shadow mask (rainbow-free
at any output size), rounded corners + vignette.

midvunit_v.cpp reads MIDV_GL_CRT=1 at boot and polls F9 (edge-triggered,
GetAsyncKeyState) for a live toggle; adds glUniform1f to the loader.
Header regenerated from gpu/renderer.py per the documented workflow.

Verified in-process at 4K: scanlines + mask visible in MIDV_GL_SNAP crops
(downscaled previews average the effect away - always inspect crops at 1:1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01M8n8qHsRWCKsJjXgqH6e98
---
