Subject: [PATCH 20/24] GL overlay: crack-fill pass (MIDV_GL_CRACKFILL, default
 on)

Scene pass gains an R8UI "written this scene" mask on attachment 1
(glDrawBuffers; mask-only glClearBufferuiv per scene so pages still
persist). The palette pass redirects pixels the scene left unwritten -
hardware quad cracks that show the stale page - to their nearest written
neighbour, only when bounded on both sides along an axis, so silhouettes
against the cleared 16:9 margins are never smeared. 3D scenes only;
radius 4*scale fine px; MIDV_GL_CRACKFILL=0 restores raw hardware.
Shaders regenerated from gpu/renderer.py (exact mode untouched -
re-verified 100.0000% on both captures).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QABHMhAzD8GxaNT8zBVLho
---
 src/mame/midway/midvunit_gl_shaders.h | 34 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 src/mame/midway/midvunit_v.cpp        | 29 +++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 62 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

